Appendix A X-Cell Model Specification
A.6 Training Validation Metrics
The following metrics are computed on a held-out validation split during training to monitor optimization and detect collapse; they are not the final held-out test metrics reported in the main text. Training validation metrics operate on pseudobulk centroids aggregated within each predicted set of S = 64 cells at the subsampled context length ( G ′ ≤ 4 , 000), and fold-changes are computed relative to the matched control set. In contrast, cell-eval test metrics (Section 4.1.8) operate on full-context predictions ( G ≈ 19k) from unseen datasets or contexts. Notably, training DE Pearson r fl attens fold-changes across all perturbations and genes into one vector before computing correlation (a single global r ), whereas celleval Pearson δ computes a per-perturbation correlation then averages. Similarly, ˆ ρ (delta norm ratio) is a training diagnostic for magnitude collapse (ˆ ρ ≪ 1) with no direct cell-eval counterpart.

